00:00:03.085 --> 00:00:11.064
If you're in need of awesome online learning platform then stick around until the end to find out more.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.963
It is New Years eve and knights of king Arthur's court enjoy the Christmas festivities with a grand feast.

00:01:06.963 --> 00:01:14.910
They exchange gifts with one another and at the request of Arthur they share stories of adventure.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:20.194
All of sudden the doors are forced upon and a mysterious figure rides down the hall.

00:01:20.194 --> 00:01:28.561
Before them is an enormous man on a green horse, with green skin, green hair and a green axe.

00:01:28.561 --> 00:01:34.011
He dismounts holding his axe in one hand a branch of holly in the other,

00:01:34.011 --> 00:01:39.843
naturally this intrusion is not taken lightly and knights of Author draw their weapons.

00:01:39.843 --> 00:01:46.404
The Green Knight laughs this off, claiming he has not come looking for a fight.

00:01:46.404 --> 00:01:52.781
Even if that was the case no man in this room would even come close to presenting a challenge for him.

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:57.181
Instead he wishes to share the festive spirit with a game.

00:01:57.181 --> 00:02:06.306
The rules of this game are fairly simple, anyone who is brave enough may strike him as hard they desire.

00:02:06.306 --> 00:02:11.310
Whoever accepts this challenge will get to keep the Knights splendid axe.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:20.397
The only condition the green knight sets is that he will return in one year and day to return this blow.

00:02:20.397 --> 00:02:30.011
A game like this would cause some hesitation, why would someone want to play a game that would surely result in their death, what’s the catch here?

00:02:30.011 --> 00:02:37.841
The knights remained weary of the situation but King Arthur was not one to shy away from a challenge and was ready to accept.

00:02:37.841 --> 00:02:43.369
However Arthur's Nephew and youngest of all the knights stepped forward.

00:02:43.369 --> 00:02:49.944
Sir Gawain accepted this challenge on behalf of Arthur eager to prove himself worthy.

00:02:49.944 --> 00:02:59.117
The Green Knight took no expectation to this, he leant over and presented his neck, almost instructing Gawain where to strike.

00:02:59.117 --> 00:03:04.598
Gawain took his blade and in swift strike beheaded the Green Knight.

00:03:04.598 --> 00:03:12.442
The young knight was  given the prestige and recognition he desired and our story ends here.

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:16.794
At least that’s what may have happened if this knight was an ordinary man.

00:03:16.794 --> 00:03:21.010
The Green Knight neither flinched or fell despite being decapitated.

00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:28.142
Instead he dropped his axe, walked over to his severed head, picked it up and faced the king and queen.

00:03:28.142 --> 00:03:37.624
“In one Year and one day we shall meet again at the Green chapel and I shall return the blow Sir Gawain.”

00:03:37.624 --> 00:03:43.843
He reminded the young knight before riding off, his sinister laugh echoing through the hall.

00:03:43.843 --> 00:03:54.360
Arthur assured his terrified wife that this was merely a light-hearted game to ease her concerns but Gawain didn’t seem as convinced.

00:03:54.360 --> 00:04:01.318
He took the axe as a trophy but also as a reminder of his promise to the green knight.

00:04:01.318 --> 00:04:11.582
As the year went by Gawain continued his duties and took part in several adventures paying little notice to what appeared to be his impending death.

00:04:11.582 --> 00:04:18.565
Eventually the day drew close and Gawain set off to meet the Green Knight in the Green Chapel.

00:04:18.565 --> 00:04:25.330
On his way he came across a magnificent castle and in the need of rest he decided to enter.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:32.598
The lord of the castle and his beautiful wife were overjoyed to have such an esteemed guest.

00:04:32.598 --> 00:04:45.634
Gawain only planned on a short rest but the lord insisted he enjoyed their hospitality until he was fully rested and ready to continue his journey as the green chapel was less than a few miles away.

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:51.429
Given what was waiting for him at the green chapel it seemed like a good idea to accept the lord's offer.

00:04:51.429 --> 00:05:04.324
The only other person of note in the castle was an old hag that Gawain assumed must have been of some importance by the respect she was given from the servants and the lord himself.

00:05:04.324 --> 00:05:10.295
The lord was a rather big fan of hunting and he made Gawain a proposal.

00:05:10.295 --> 00:05:20.044
Every day the lord went out hunting, he would give Gawain what he caught. On the condition that Gawain would give him whatever he gained while he was gone.

00:05:20.044 --> 00:05:29.418
He accepted the lord's challenge and when he set off for his daily hunt, Gawain was left to explore the castle grounds and rest.

00:05:29.418 --> 00:05:33.107
However his day would present it’s own challenges,

00:05:33.107 --> 00:05:42.159
the lords wife began with some subtle flirtation and so in order to avoid an uncomfortable situation Gawain retreated to his chambers.

00:05:42.159 --> 00:05:54.037
Unfortunately she followed and continued her seduction, trying his best not to offend his hostess but also respect his host; he allowed the lord’s wife a single kiss.

00:05:54.037 --> 00:06:03.511
When the lord returned he presented Gawain with a deer he had killed and in return he received a kiss but Gawain didn’t mention where this kiss came from.

00:06:03.511 --> 00:06:15.363
The next day the lord set out for his hunt, once again Gawain rejected the advances from the lord’s wife, this time He was given two kisses.

00:06:15.363 --> 00:06:25.222
The lord returned with a boar for Gawain, in exchange he is given two kisses and again he doesn’t tell the lord where they came from.

00:06:25.222 --> 00:06:37.056
The third day begins with the Lord setting off for his hunt, however when Gawain rejects the advances of his hostess this time she gives him a golden ring to remember her by.

00:06:37.056 --> 00:06:42.150
Even this is rejected by Gawain but the lord's wife insisted he accept her sash.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:49.213
A wonderful green and gold sash that was enchanted to protect the wearer from any physical harm.

00:06:49.213 --> 00:06:56.453
This item Gawain accepted after all there is a giant Green Knight eager to decapitate him.

00:06:56.453 --> 00:07:04.620
Gawain is then given three kisses and made to promise he will keep this gift secret from husband.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:16.206
When the Lord returns he presents Gawain a fox this time and in exchange he was given three kisses but Gawain doesn’t mention the sash given to him.

00:07:16.206 --> 00:07:27.394
The next morning is the day Gawain must travel to the Green Chapel, he ties the sash around his belt and least now there is a chance that may survive the encounter.

00:07:27.394 --> 00:07:32.991
When he arrives at the chapel the Green Knight is already there sharpening his axe.

00:07:32.991 --> 00:07:40.973
Gawain hesitantly walks over and as a part of their deal presents his neck and prepares to receive his blow.

00:07:40.973 --> 00:07:47.939
The Knight pulls back his axe and swings, but stops just short as Gawain flinches.

00:07:47.939 --> 00:07:54.115
The Knight laughs telling Gawain he thought the knights of Arthur feared nothing.

00:07:54.115 --> 00:08:01.733
The second time the Green Knight pulls back his axe Gawain bites down and doesn’t flinch.

00:08:01.733 --> 00:08:15.645
The blow he receives however most definitely doesn’t match the one given, strangely Gawain is angry at the Knight for holding back and berates him until he does strike him at full force.

00:08:15.645 --> 00:08:23.642
Luckily for Gawain the sash given him appeared to have worked as the strike only left behind a small wound.

00:08:23.642 --> 00:08:31.911
Gawain prepared to leave believing the Knight’s game was over, but he towered over Gawain laughing and when challenged.

00:08:31.911 --> 00:08:40.319
He revealed himself as lord Bertilak the exact same lord of the castle Gawain had been a guest of.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:51.222
He was transformed into the Green Knight with the use of magic, the old woman he noticed earlier was in fact the sorceress Morgan Le Fey in disguise.

00:08:51.222 --> 00:08:56.928
She planned this entire game as a way of testing the honour of King Arthur's Knights.

00:08:56.928 --> 00:09:11.786
The axe would have never caused Gawain any harm but because he failed to present Bertilak with the sash his wife had given him, the wound from the third strike would be ever present, a scar that marked his dishonesty.

00:09:11.786 --> 00:09:18.098
Gawain kneels in shame for his deceit but the Green Knight laughs it off and tells him to stand.

00:09:18.098 --> 00:09:30.998
Reminding him not to hold himself to such unrealistic standards, the fact he honoured his end of the bargain was enough for the Green Knight to call him the most blameless Knight in all the land.

00:09:30.998 --> 00:09:38.974
Gawain returned to Camelot wearing the sash, a symbol of his failure to keep his promise.

00:09:38.974 --> 00:09:47.947
In honour of Gawain’s adventure the knights agree to all wear a green sash as a reminder to always be honest.

00:09:47.947 --> 00:09:58.373
The story of Sir Gawain and the Green Knight is classed as a Chivalric Romance, it was written towards the end of the 14th century and we don’t know who the author was.

00:09:58.373 --> 00:10:03.139
The story also had no title until several centuries later.

00:10:03.139 --> 00:10:13.049
Surprisingly at the time it was written the poem was received very poorly, whereas today it’s a highly revered story that has been studied and adapted in numerous forms.

00:10:13.049 --> 00:10:19.533
One of the most famous examples being a translation of the poem by none other than Tolkien himself.

00:10:19.533 --> 00:10:31.415
What inspired me to go back over this story and make this video was the modern film adaptation that is scheduled to be released around August of this year which is titled The Green Knight.

00:10:31.415 --> 00:10:45.324
Watching the trailer I really like the design of the Green Knight himself but given Hollywood's track record when it comes to adapting classic stories I’m about as optimistic as a man about to be beheaded by a giant Green Knight

00:10:45.324 --> 00:10:49.294
but I’d love to be surprised.

